--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -43,3 +43,16 @@ Start the development server:
 ```sh
 bin/dev
 ```
+
+## Erasing a user
+
+An administrator can use **Remove** in the user list. Books the person created with
+“everyone” access keep their content and get the byline “Deleted author”. Other
+books they created are deleted, even if published. Unreferenced attached files
+are purged by the background worker after commit.
+
+Previously deactivated users aren't on the list. For an individual erasure
+request, look up and verify the inactive user's ID, then run
+`User.where(active: false).find(id).destroy!` in the Rails console. This uses the
+same erasure as Remove. Don't select by original email alone: someone else may
+have registered with it since deactivation.
